# Context Architecture

## Requirements

- [!] This project uses the hierarchical agent context tree from the context-tree convention (`specs/workspace/standards/context-tree.spec.md`).
  - **Root AGENTS.md** (30-40KB): compressed methodology with routing to sub-agents
  - **ctxt/** (flat, 4-10KB each): define.md, design.md, evolve.md, session.md, msl-audit.md, audit.md; no phases/ or utils/ subfolders
  - **ctxt/domains/**: domain specialists from the taxonomy classification
  - **Proactive loading**: the agent decides what context to load from the task
  - **Regeneration**: `/livespec:audit context`

- [!] This project defines what content populates agent contexts to ensure focused, relevant guidance.

  **Content Sources** (what feeds AGENTS.md generation):

  Always Include (root AGENTS.md):
  - specs/workspace/constitution.spec.md - Development principles
  - specs/workspace/patterns.spec.md - Naming conventions
  - specs/workspace/workflows.spec.md - Phase guidance
  - Key behaviors from specs/features/ relevant to daily work

  Include When Relevant (sub-agent contexts):
  - Phase-specific behaviors when agent determines phase work
  - Domain-specific patterns when taxonomy indicates
  - Session and audit workflows when completing sessions or checking spec health

  Exclude:
  - Detailed implementation specs (reference, don't inline)
  - Contract definitions (link to specs/interfaces/ instead)
  - Historical/archived content
  - Paths that exist only in the LiveSpec toolchain: generated context must work without it

  Compression Level: as declared by `context_compression` in constitution.spec.md

  **Structural Hints**:

  Root AGENTS.md Priorities (ordering):
  1. Spec-first enforcement (most critical)
  2. Core principles from constitution
  3. Patterns and conventions
  4. Key behaviors for daily work
  5. Sub-agent routing table

  Sub-Agent Triggers (keyword → context mapping):
  - "new project", "setup", "define", "constraints" → ctxt/define.md
  - "design", "architecture", "behaviors", "contracts" → ctxt/design.md
  - "implement", "build", "test", "verify", "drift", "evolve" → ctxt/evolve.md
  - "complete session", "measure compliance" → ctxt/session.md
  - "audit MSL", "minimalism", "spec quality" → ctxt/msl-audit.md
  - "health", "validation", "context regeneration" → ctxt/audit.md

  **Content Focus** (balanced mix):
  - Behaviors: 40% - Observable outcomes from specs/features/
  - Constraints: 30% - Requirements from specs/foundation/
  - Patterns: 30% - Workspace methodology from specs/workspace/

- [!] Every source maps to the generated file(s) it feeds, so a change can be regenerated in scope rather than in full
  - `/livespec:audit context` reads this map to classify a change as MINOR or FULL; without it every rebuild runs in full

  **Spec → Generated File Map:**

  | Source | Generated File(s) | Structural? |
  |--------|-------------------|-------------|
  | PURPOSE.md | AGENTS.md § Summary | No |
  | constitution.spec.md | AGENTS.md § Core Principles | Compression-level changes are structural (affect every file) |
  | patterns.spec.md | AGENTS.md § Patterns and conventions; ctxt/domains/*.md | No |
  | workflows.spec.md | AGENTS.md § Phases; ctxt/define.md, ctxt/design.md, ctxt/evolve.md | No |
  | taxonomy.spec.md | AGENTS.md § Folder organisation; ctxt/domains/*.md | Domain classification changes are structural (add/remove domain files) |
  | context-architecture.spec.md (this spec) | Tree structure itself: which files exist, size budgets, load triggers | Always structural |
  | foundation/*.spec.md | AGENTS.md § Summary; § Core Principles | No |
  | features/*.spec.md | AGENTS.md § key behaviors; Reference Library | No |
  | strategy/*.spec.md | *(none)* unless AGENTS.md inlines it; then name the section | No |
  | interfaces/*.spec.md | *(none)* unless AGENTS.md describes the external system; then name the section | No |

  Every spec is a staleness source, so a spec missing from this map forces a full rebuild until it is listed. Add a row for every other workspace spec this project has. **Structural** means the change can add, remove or resize generated files beyond the mapped targets, so it forces a full rebuild. A source that feeds no generated file is listed with *(none)* as its target and does not force a full rebuild.

## Validation

- Root AGENTS.md within the convention budget (30-40KB)
- ctxt/ is flat plus ctxt/domains/, with no phases/ or utils/ subfolders
- Load triggers functional (agent matches query to sub-agent)
- Context generation reads this spec before building AGENTS.md
- Always-include content appears in root context
- Sub-agent triggers route to files that exist
- Excluded content not inlined (referenced only)
- Compression level matches constitution.spec.md declaration
- Every workspace spec appears as a source in the Spec → Generated File Map
